IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`
IMPORT `vmu-s03-definitions`
IMPORT `vmu-s04-s05-values`
IMPORT `vmu-s06-s07-notification-and-calculation`
IMPORT `vmu-s08-construction`
IMPORT `vmu-s09-regulations`
IMPORT `vmu-s10-notification`
IMPORT `vmu-s11-s12-2012-and-sla`

-- Monetary Units Act 2004 (Victoria), sections 1 to 12 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person or agency that sets, indexes or applies a Victorian fee or penalty.
-- The questions are what a fee unit or a penalty unit is worth in a financial year, how an amount stated in units converts to dollars and is rounded,
-- and when the values must be notified. Nothing here is new law: each question calls a rule of the layer-1 modules imported above.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list), one for each fact the person can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. The records and the optional values that the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question from those answers.
-- A fact that a rule asks as "if any" is asked as two inputs: whether there is one, and what it is (0 when there is none).
-- Where the person's answer is a number the text does not state (the amount the Treasurer fixed, the annual rate), the layer asks for it: a later notice would change the answer.
--
-- An answer that is NOTHING means the text does not answer on those facts; JUST FALSE means the text itself says no.
-- There is no seat for the Treasurer or the Minister: their duties appear here only as what they mean to the person asking.
--
-- Financial years are named by the calendar year in which they start on 1 July: the financial year starting on 1 July 2025 is 2025.
-- For the financial year starting on 1 July 2012 the values and the annual rate are stated by section 11 "Despite sections 5 and 6"; the by-what-day questions answer NOTHING for that year,
-- because the text does not say whether the notice and the fixing are still due.
-- The annual rate is asked as a proportion: 2.5% is 0.025, as section 11(3) states it.
-- Sections 5(6) and (7) raise the previous value by it (the previous value times one plus the rate), and sections 9(1)(g) and (2)(h) add it to 1 and compound it;
-- every function called here takes the rate as that proportion.
-- Amounts are in dollars, as the text writes "$".

§ `Monetary Units Act 2004 (Victoria) -- the questions of a person who sets, indexes or applies a fee or penalty`

§§ `Meaning of fee and penalty (s 3)`

-- s 3. "fee includes charge or other amount".
@export Is this a fee for the purposes of the Act (s 3)?
GIVEN `it is a fee in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a fee in the ordinary sense of the word?
      `it is a charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a charge?
      `it is an other amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it some other amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a fee for the purposes of the Act` IS
    `s 3 -- the item is a fee` `it is a fee in the ordinary sense` `it is a charge` `it is an other amount`

-- s 3. "penalty means a fine or other monetary penalty and includes an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule in respect of an offence for which an infringement notice can be issued under the Act".
@export Is this a penalty for the purposes of the Act (s 3)?
GIVEN `it is a fine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a fine?
      `it is another monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it another monetary penalty?
      `it is an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an amount payable under an Act or a statutory rule?
      `it is payable in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable in respect of an offence?
      `an infringement notice can be issued for that offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can an infringement notice be issued for that offence under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a penalty for the purposes of the Act` IS
    `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` `it is a fine` `it is another monetary penalty` `it is an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule` `it is payable in respect of an offence` `an infringement notice can be issued for that offence under the Act`

§§ `Fee units in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument (s 4)`

-- s 4. A statement of a number of fee units in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument must, unless the context otherwise requires,
-- be construed as stating that number of dollars, the product with the amount fixed.
@export How many dollars does a statement of fee units state (s 4)?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument that holds the statement` IS AN Instrument @desc Where is the statement of fee units made: in an Act, in a statutory rule, in a legislative instrument, or in an instrument of another kind?
      `the context requires the statement to be read otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the statement require it to be read otherwise than as a number of dollars?
      `the number of fee units` IS A NUMBER @desc How many fee units does the statement give? (It may be whole, fractional or decimal.)
      `the amount the Treasurer fixed for one fee unit` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, did the Treasurer fix for one fee unit under section 5(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many dollars does a statement of fee units state` IS
    `s 4 -- the number of dollars a statement of fee units states, where the section applies` `the kind of instrument that holds the statement` `the context requires the statement to be read otherwise` `the number of fee units` `the amount the Treasurer fixed for one fee unit`

§§ `What a fee unit, a penalty unit and the annual rate are worth (ss 5, 11)`

-- ss 5(1), 11(1)(a), 11(2). The value of a fee unit is the amount the Treasurer fixes for the financial year by notice in the Government Gazette,
-- except that for the financial year starting on 1 July 2012 the Act itself states the value.
@export What is a fee unit worth, in dollars, for a financial year (ss 5(1), 11(1)(a), 11(2))?
GIVEN `the year in which the financial year starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the financial year start? (The year of its 1 July: for the financial year starting on 1 July 2025, enter 2025.)
      `a notice fixing the fee unit was published in the Government Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Treasurer fix the value of a fee unit for that financial year by a notice published in the Government Gazette?
      `the amount the notice fixed for one fee unit` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, did that notice fix for one fee unit? (0 if there was no notice.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is a fee unit worth for the financial year` IS
    `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` `the year in which the financial year starts` `a notice fixing the fee unit was published in the Government Gazette` `the amount the notice fixed for one fee unit`

-- ss 5(2), 11(1)(b), 11(2). The same for a penalty unit.
@export What is a penalty unit worth, in dollars, for a financial year (ss 5(2), 11(1)(b), 11(2))?
GIVEN `the year in which the financial year starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the financial year start? (The year of its 1 July: for the financial year starting on 1 July 2025, enter 2025.)
      `a notice fixing the penalty unit was published in the Government Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Treasurer fix the value of a penalty unit for that financial year by a notice published in the Government Gazette?
      `the amount the notice fixed for one penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, did that notice fix for one penalty unit? (0 if there was no notice.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is a penalty unit worth for the financial year` IS
    `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` `the year in which the financial year starts` `a notice fixing the penalty unit was published in the Government Gazette` `the amount the notice fixed for one penalty unit`

-- ss 5(4), 11(3). The annual rate for the financial year starting on 1 July in a year is to be fixed before 1 March of that year;
-- for the financial year starting on 1 July 2012 the Act states the rate itself "Despite section 5", and the text does not say whether it is still to be fixed, so the answer is NOTHING.
@export By what day must the annual rate for a financial year be fixed (ss 5(4), 11(3))?
GIVEN `the year in which the financial year starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the financial year start? (The year of its 1 July.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the annual rate be fixed` IS
    `s 11(3) -- the last day on which the annual rate may be fixed, for the financial year` `the year in which the financial year starts`

-- ss 5(4), 5(5), 11(3), 11(4). The annual rate is the one fixed for the year; if none was fixed it is the one determined for the year before;
-- for the financial year starting on 1 July 2012 the Act itself states it.
@export What is the annual rate for a financial year (ss 5(4), 5(5), 11(3), 11(4))?
GIVEN `the year in which the financial year starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the financial year start? (The year of its 1 July.)
      `the Treasurer fixed an annual rate for that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Treasurer fix an annual rate for that financial year under section 5(4)?
      `the annual rate the Treasurer fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc What annual rate did the Treasurer fix, as a proportion (2.5% is 0.025)? (0 if none was fixed.)
      `an annual rate was determined for the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an annual rate determined for the financial year before?
      `the annual rate determined for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What annual rate was determined for the financial year before, as a proportion (2.5% is 0.025)? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the annual rate for the financial year` IS
    `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` `the year in which the financial year starts` `the rate fixed` `the previous rate`
    WHERE
        `the rate fixed` MEANS IF `the Treasurer fixed an annual rate for that financial year` THEN JUST `the annual rate the Treasurer fixed` ELSE NOTHING
        `the previous rate` MEANS IF `an annual rate was determined for the previous financial year` THEN JUST `the annual rate determined for the previous financial year` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 5(6). A fee unit fixed for a year must not exceed the product of the previous year's value and the annual rate, rounded to the nearest cent.
@export What is the amount that section 5(6) compares a new fee unit with (s 5(6))?
GIVEN `the value of a fee unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of one fee unit, in dollars, in the previous financial year?
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the annual rate for the financial year in which the new fee unit is to apply? (Enter it as a proportion: 2.5% is 0.025.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the amount that section 5(6) compares a new fee unit with` IS
    `s 5(6) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent` `the value of a fee unit in the previous financial year` `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply`

@export Is a proposed fee unit above what section 5(6) allows (s 5(6))?
GIVEN `the amount of the fee unit proposed` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, has been proposed for one fee unit?
      `the value of a fee unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of one fee unit, in dollars, in the previous financial year?
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the annual rate for the financial year in which the new fee unit is to apply? (Enter it as a proportion: 2.5% is 0.025.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a proposed fee unit above what section 5(6) allows` IS
    `s 5(6) -- the amount of the fee unit fixed exceeds the amount the subsection allows` `the amount of the fee unit proposed` `the value of a fee unit in the previous financial year` `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply`

-- s 5(7). The same for a penalty unit.
@export What is the amount that section 5(7) compares a new penalty unit with (s 5(7))?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of one penalty unit, in dollars, in the previous financial year?
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the annual rate for the financial year in which the new penalty unit is to apply? (Enter it as a proportion: 2.5% is 0.025.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the amount that section 5(7) compares a new penalty unit with` IS
    `s 5(7) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent` `the value of a penalty unit in the previous financial year` `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply`

@export Is a proposed penalty unit above what section 5(7) allows (s 5(7))?
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty unit proposed` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, has been proposed for one penalty unit?
      `the value of a penalty unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of one penalty unit, in dollars, in the previous financial year?
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the annual rate for the financial year in which the new penalty unit is to apply? (Enter it as a proportion: 2.5% is 0.025.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a proposed penalty unit above what section 5(7) allows` IS
    `s 5(7) -- the amount of the penalty unit fixed exceeds the amount the subsection allows` `the amount of the penalty unit proposed` `the value of a penalty unit in the previous financial year` `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply`

§§ `When the values must be notified (ss 6, 11)`

-- ss 6, 11(1). Before 1 June each year notice of the values for the financial year starting on 1 July that year is to be published;
-- for the financial year starting on 1 July 2012 the Act states the values itself "Despite sections 5 and 6", and the text does not say whether the notice is still due, so the answer is NOTHING.
@export By what day must notice of the fee unit and penalty unit values for a financial year be published (ss 6, 11(1))?
GIVEN `the year in which the financial year starts` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the financial year start? (The year of its 1 July.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must notice of the values be published` IS
    `s 11(1) -- the last day on which notice of the values may be published, for the financial year` `the year in which the financial year starts`

§§ `Converting an amount stated in units to dollars (s 7)`

-- s 7(1). A fee stated by a fee unit in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument is the number of units times the value of a fee unit.
@export How many dollars is a fee stated as a number of fee units (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument that states the fee` IS AN Instrument @desc Where is the fee stated: in an Act, in a statutory rule, in a legislative instrument, or in an instrument of another kind?
      `the number of fee units applicable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many fee units is the fee? (It may be whole, fractional or decimal.)
      `the value of a fee unit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of one fee unit, in dollars, for the financial year in which the fee applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many dollars is a fee stated as a number of fee units` IS
    `s 7(1) -- the amount of the fee, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `the kind of instrument that states the fee` `the number of fee units applicable` `the value of a fee unit`

-- s 7(2). A penalty stated by a penalty unit in an Act or a statutory rule is the number of units times the value of a penalty unit.
@export How many dollars is a penalty stated as a number of penalty units (s 7(2))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument that states the penalty` IS AN Instrument @desc Where is the penalty stated: in an Act, in a statutory rule, in a legislative instrument, or in an instrument of another kind?
      `the number of penalty units applicable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many penalty units is the penalty? (It may be whole, fractional or decimal.)
      `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of one penalty unit, in dollars, for the financial year in which the penalty applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many dollars is a penalty stated as a number of penalty units` IS
    `s 7(2) -- the amount of the penalty, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `the kind of instrument that states the penalty` `the number of penalty units applicable` `the value of a penalty unit`

-- s 7(3). The amount calculated under section 7 may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
@export To what amount may a fee stated in fee units be rounded (s 7(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument that states the fee` IS AN Instrument @desc Where is the fee stated: in an Act, in a statutory rule, in a legislative instrument, or in an instrument of another kind?
      `the number of fee units applicable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many fee units is the fee? (It may be whole, fractional or decimal.)
      `the value of a fee unit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of one fee unit, in dollars, for the financial year in which the fee applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `To what amount may a fee stated in fee units be rounded` IS
    `s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `the kind of instrument that states the fee` `the number of fee units applicable` `the value of a fee unit`

-- s 7(4). The amount calculated under section 7 may be rounded to the nearest dollar.
@export To what amount may a penalty stated in penalty units be rounded (s 7(4))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument that states the penalty` IS AN Instrument @desc Where is the penalty stated: in an Act, in a statutory rule, in a legislative instrument, or in an instrument of another kind?
      `the number of penalty units applicable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many penalty units is the penalty? (It may be whole, fractional or decimal.)
      `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of one penalty unit, in dollars, for the financial year in which the penalty applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `To what amount may a penalty stated in penalty units be rounded` IS
    `s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `the kind of instrument that states the penalty` `the number of penalty units applicable` `the value of a penalty unit`

§§ `What may be construed in units (s 8)`

-- s 8(1). A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes a fee may be construed as authorising the fee by reference to a fee unit.
@export Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `the provision is in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision in an Act?
      `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision authorise the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule?
      `the statutory rule prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that statutory rule prescribe, fix or charge a fee, however expressed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units` IS
    `s 8(1) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `the provision is in an Act` `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule` `the statutory rule prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed`

-- s 8(1A). The same for an instrument maker making a legislative instrument, under a provision in an Act or a statutory rule.
@export Can a power to make a legislative instrument that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units (s 8(1A))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument that holds the provision` IS AN Instrument @desc Is the provision in an Act, in a statutory rule, in a legislative instrument, or in an instrument of another kind?
      `the provision authorises an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision authorise an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument?
      `the legislative instrument prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that legislative instrument prescribe, fix or charge a fee, however expressed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a power to make a legislative instrument that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units` IS
    `s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `the kind of instrument that holds the provision` `the provision authorises an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument` `the legislative instrument prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed`

-- s 8(2). A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes a penalty for an offence against the rule may be construed as authorising it by reference to a penalty unit.
@export Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a penalty be read as a power to fix it in penalty units (s 8(2))?
GIVEN `the provision is in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision in an Act?
      `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision authorise the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule?
      `the statutory rule prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule, however expressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that statutory rule prescribe a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule, however expressed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a penalty be read as a power to fix it in penalty units` IS
    `s 8(2) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the penalty by reference to a penalty unit` `the provision is in an Act` `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule` `the statutory rule prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule, however expressed`

§§ `Regulations that convert amounts to units (s 9)`

-- s 9(2)(a). Where a regulation converts a fee in dollars into fee units: on or before 1 July 2004 the fee is divided by 10 dollars,
-- after that day by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3).
@export How many fee units is a fee in dollars when a regulation converts it (s 9(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the amount of the fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the fee, in dollars?
      `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the regulation take effect?
      `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of one fee unit, in dollars, fixed by the Treasurer? (Used only for a regulation taking effect after 1 July 2004.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many fee units is a fee in dollars when a regulation converts it` IS
    `s 9(2)(a) -- the number of fee units to which the regulation converts the fee` `the amount of the fee, in dollars` `the day on which the regulation takes effect` `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`

-- s 9(2)(b). The same for a penalty: 100 dollars on or before 1 July 2004, the value of a penalty unit after.
@export How many penalty units is a penalty in dollars when a regulation converts it (s 9(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the penalty, in dollars?
      `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the regulation take effect?
      `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of one penalty unit, in dollars, fixed by the Treasurer? (Used only for a regulation taking effect after 1 July 2004.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many penalty units is a penalty in dollars when a regulation converts it` IS
    `s 9(2)(b) -- the number of penalty units to which the regulation converts the penalty` `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` `the day on which the regulation takes effect` `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`

-- s 9(3). A number of fee units or penalty units rounded up to the next 2 decimal places is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(a) or (b).
@export What is a number of units rounded up to the next 2 decimal places (s 9(3))?
GIVEN `the number of fee units or penalty units calculated` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of fee units or penalty units did you calculate?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is a number of units rounded up to the next 2 decimal places` IS
    `s 9(3) -- the number rounded up to the next 2 decimal places` `the number of fee units or penalty units calculated`

§§ `Notice of the dollar amounts (s 10)`

-- s 10(1). The Minister responsible for an Act or statutory rule that provides for fees or penalties by units must take reasonable steps to have
-- the dollar amounts notified to the public or to the sector likely to be affected.
-- Asked by someone who applies the instrument, about the Minister who administers it: the layer-1 rule asks whether the person is that Minister,
-- and here the question is about that Minister, so the fact is passed as TRUE.
@export Must the Minister who administers the instrument I apply take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts of its fees and penalties notified (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument that provides for the fees or penalties` IS AN Instrument @desc Is the instrument that provides for the fees or penalties an Act, a statutory rule, a legislative instrument, or an instrument of another kind?
      `the instrument provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument provide for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister who administers the instrument take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts notified` IS
    `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `the kind of instrument that provides for the fees or penalties` `the instrument provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units` TRUE

-- s 10(2). The same, for fees only, where the Act or statutory rule is one under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units.
@export Must the Minister who administers the Act or statutory rule under which a legislative instrument sets my fee take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts of fees notified (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument under which the legislative instrument is made` IS AN Instrument @desc Is the instrument under which the legislative instrument is made an Act, a statutory rule, a legislative instrument, or an instrument of another kind?
      `a legislative instrument made under it provides for fees by fee units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a legislative instrument made under it provide for fees by fee units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister who administers the instrument take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts of fees in a legislative instrument notified` IS
    `s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` `the kind of instrument under which the legislative instrument is made` `a legislative instrument made under it provides for fees by fee units` TRUE

§§ `The Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 (s 12)`

-- s 12. Nothing in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing of a fee unit, a penalty unit or an annual rate in accordance with section 5 or 11.
@export Does the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 apply to the fixing of a unit or an annual rate (s 12)?
GIVEN `what is fixed` IS A `Thing fixed` @desc What is being fixed: a fee unit, a penalty unit, an annual rate, or something else?
      `it is fixed in accordance with section 5 or 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it fixed in accordance with section 5 or section 11 of the Monetary Units Act 2004?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 apply to the fixing of a unit or an annual rate` IS
    `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `what is fixed` `it is fixed in accordance with section 5 or 11`
